.TH KINTSUGI-NEW 1 "2026-10-22" "kintsugi 0.8.0" "Kintsugi Manual"
.SH NAME
kintsugi-new \- scaffold a project from a blueprint
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kintsugi new
[<blueprint>] <dir> [\-\-force]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Scaffold a new project from a blueprint. Blueprints provide templates for
different project types.
.SH OPTIONS
.IP \fB\-\-force\fR
Overwrite existing directory
.SH EXAMPLES
Create a new project:
.PP
  $ kintsugi new myproject
.PP
Use a specific blueprint:
.PP
  $ kintsugi new c2 myproject
  $ kintsugi new detection my-detector
  $ kintsugi new redteam my-tooling
.PP
Force overwrite:
.PP
  $ kintsugi new --force myproject
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR kintsugi (1),
.BR kintsugi-init (1)
